.TH "YAMLR-ROLLBACK" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-rollback \- Atomic reversal of the last remediation session.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr rollback [PATH] [FLAGS]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fByamlr-rollback\fR restores manifests to their exact pre-mutation state from the most recent remediation session.
.PP
Every time \fByamlr heal\fR, \fByamlr upgrade\fR, \fByamlr fmt\fR, or \fByamlr secure\fR alters a manifest, an atomic SHA-256 verified backup snapshot is stored in \fB.yamlr/backups/\fR. Invoking \fBrollback\fR restores all affected files in the target directory immediately.
.PP
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fBPATH\fR
Target manifest file or directory containing the workspace (defaults to current directory \fB.\fR).
.SH "FLAGS"
.TP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
Show precision command help and options.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.TP
Revert workspace to state before last heal session:
.B yamlr rollback
.TP
Revert specific target folder:
.B yamlr rollback ./deploy
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR yamlr (1),
.BR yamlr-restore (1),
.BR yamlr-heal (1)
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/yamlr/yamlr/issues>
.PP
